by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-30T22:11:01Z

Pushed a change on top: reading the attribute no longer clears it, and the flag is gone.

With the removal you added in `onAuthenticationSuccess()`, consuming it on read only costs the retry: one mistyped password and the second render of the login page no longer knows it is a re-authentication. The error and the last username both survive that, because the framework rewrites them on every failed attempt, while this one is written once by `startReAuthentication()`. That left `false` as the only correct value for the flag, so it seemed better not to have one.

Lifecycle is the authenticator's now: set on start, cleared on success, cleared on logout.
